&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an Implementation Engineer to own the successful delivery of Forter integrations for newly signed and expanding customers. This is a project management-led role: you are the delivery owner for your portfolio, responsible for driving each integration from kickoff to go-live on time, with strong stakeholder alignment and a clear line of sight to business value for the customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll bring the organisational rigor and proactive ownership that turns a complex, multi-stakeholder go-live into a predictable, repeatable process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end delivery of integration projects for your portfolio, acting as project lead and primary point of contact from kickoff through go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and drive project plans to completion, proactively identifying risks and blockers and course-correcting before they threaten timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead project governance with customer stakeholders, setting agendas, tracking action items, and managing relationships with senior stakeholders and business users to keep them engaged and aligned through completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functionally with Sales, Solutions Consulting, Customer Success, and Analytics, including partnering with an Analytics Consultant to translate technical integration progress into insights that meet customers&#39; fraud prevention needs, to remove obstacles and hit agreed go-live dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a technical translator on your projects, clearly articulating integration concepts (API operations, JavaScript, JSON, and other web/database technologies) to technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on project health and delivery metrics for your portfolio, flagging risks early in team meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the continuous improvement of Forter&#39;s implementation playbooks and processes, feeding back learnings from your projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder projects on behalf of Enterprise customers, including engaging senior customer stakeholders and holding cross-functional teams accountable; project/program management experience is the core requirement for this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record running multiple concurrent projects, building structured project plans, and driving them to on-time completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organisational skills and attention to detail, with a consistent focus on delivery quality and customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An owner&#39;s mindset: proactive, accountable, and comfortable driving a project forward without being told to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluency in Mandarin and English is essential for this position.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working technical fluency with API integrations, JavaScript, JSON concepts, and other web/database technologies, enough to bridge technical and business conversations; hands-on build experience is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a multinational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in payments or ecommerce is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in data analysis tools (SQL, Python) and experience with customer segmentation or large dataset trend analysis is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
