&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Forter is some of the internet&#39;s biggest eCommerce merchants&#39; trust platform. We help them sell more by lowering the friction that fraud and abuse add to the buying experience, and that means making a lot of decisions for them. We process over 10M daily decisions for an annual GMV of over $500B. The Decision Engineering team owns the core of this business value proposition: Forter&#39;s decision engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The engine is committed to maintaining a strict latency SLA (p99&amp;lt;500ms) and a 5-nines availability rating. For each decision we run an unusually large data enrichment topology that encapsulates the combined and accumulated knowledge of Forter&#39;s analytical staff and upstream cyber capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The team lives in a highly technical backend domain, where the roadmap is composed of product-led and engineering-led initiatives in roughly equal parts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Along with the engine itself, the team owns the API entry point into Forter, and the development process that allows analysts to build the engine using a self-service approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The team is extremely central in Forter&#39;s business day-to-day, and many of the challenges in the team arise from that centrality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To hear more about engine development at Forter, why it&#39;s interesting and what&#39;s the difference between an engine and an infrastructure, we talked about exactly that on the Hebrew language podcast עושים תוכנה: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oqbFRDH5GEQ&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Given that the role requires active participation in the roadmap setting, you will need an investor &quot;tool-set&quot; that includes developing a solid and nuanced understanding of Forter&#39;s business value and the ability to zoom in/out on the details (including technical details) while always keeping an eye on ROI and risk. You&#39;ll need to be an innovator in spirit, that knows the power of a simple and well thought out piece of software to solve big business problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own one of Forter&#39;s most business-critical areas. Oversee its development to ensure SLAs and long-term quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide top-tier engineers (including Staff+) on how to plan and execute projects that carry a lot of technical risk (risk of ballooning investments) and precision/product risk (bad ROI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide engineers on how to develop their business-value understanding, and how to channel their innovation towards the places that move the needle the most from a business perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate around the engine&#39;s capabilities, APIs and the agentic interfaces that it offers Forter customers. Be opinionated around the engine&#39;s product-space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing business critical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IC experience as Staff+ Engineer or Tech Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing big projects that have technical and/or business risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in performance critical environments (high scale, demanding SLAs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
